otice is needed.`:`Month-to-month: begins ${r(`start_date`)} and continues month to month.`,i(`early_move_in`)&&`Early move-in: Tenant may move in on ${r(`early_move_in_date`)}. Rent for those days is ${r(`early_move_in_rent`)}.`,`After a fixed term ends: if Tenant stays more than one week after the end date and neither party has objected in writing, the lease continues month to month on these same terms. Either party may end a month-to-month lease with written notice at least ${r(`monthly_notice_days`)} days before the end of a monthly period. To prevent the automatic month-to-month, either party may give written notice before the end date that the lease will not continue.`),o(`3. Rent`,`Rent is ${r(`rent_amount`)} per month, due in advance on the ${zn(n(`rent_due_day`))} day of each month. Pay by ${r(`pay_methods`)} to ${r(`payee`)}. The first month's rent of ${r(`first_rent_amount`)} is due ${r(`first_rent_due`)}. Rent for a partial first month is ${r(`partial_month`)}. See the Payment Schedule at the end.`),o(`4. Late fee and returned payments`,`Rent is late if not received in full by the end of the ${zn(n(`late_after_day`))} day of the month. A late fee of ${r(`late_fee`)} is then due.`+(i(`daily_late`)?` Starting the ${zn(String(Number(n(`late_after_day`))+1))} day, an additional ${r(`daily_late_amount`)} per day is due until rent is paid.`:``)+` The total late fees for any one month will never exceed ${r(`late_fee_cap`)}.`,`A payment returned unpaid (for example, a bounced check or reversed transfer) incurs a fee of ${r(`returned_payment_fee`)}, plus any late fee.`),o(`5. Security deposit`,`Tenant pays a refundable security deposit of ${r(`deposit_amount`)}, due ${r(`deposit_due`)}.`,`- Return: Landlord returns the deposit within one month after the lease ends and Tenant gives back possession and keys.`,`- Deductions: Landlord may keep only what is reasonably needed to cover unpaid rent or other amounts Tenant owes under this lease, or damage beyond normal wear and tear. If Landlord keeps any part, Landlord sends an itemized written list of what was kept and why, within one month after the lease ends (Louisiana law allows up to 15 more days after that month).`,`- Forwarding address: Tenant gives Landlord a forwarding address in writing at move-out.`,`- Not last month's rent: Tenant may not use the deposit as rent unless Landlord agrees in writing.`,`- Abandonment: if Tenant abandons the Home before the lease ends, or without giving the notice this lease requires, the one-month return rule does not apply. Landlord will still account for the deposit.`,`- Sale of the Home: if the Home is sold, Landlord transfers the deposit to the new owner, who becomes responsible for returning it.`),o(`6. Utilities and services`,`Tenant pays for and puts in Tenant's name, effective on move-in: ${r(`tenant_utilities`)}. Landlord pays for: ${r(`landlord_utilities`)}. Tenant keeps utilities on through move-out, including heat in freezing weather.`),o(`7. Who lives here; guests`,`Only Tenant and these occupants may live in the Home: ${r(`occupants`)}. A guest may stay no more than ${r(`guest_days_row`)} days in a row or ${r(`guest_days_six_months`)} days in any 6 months without Landlord's written OK, which Landlord will not unreasonably refuse.`,`Emergency contact (not living in the Home): ${r(`emergency_contact`)}.`),o(`8. Furnishings and appliances`,`The Home is ${r(`furnishings`)}. Landlord provides these appliances, which stay Landlord's property: ${r(`appliances`)}. Tenant supplies: ${r(`tenant_supplies`)}.`,i(`as_is`)&&`"As-is" appliances (INITIALED by both parties): Landlord does not promise to repair or replace these specific items if they fail: ${r(`as_is_items`)}. This does NOT apply to any problem that seriously affects health or safety, or to any defect Landlord knew or should have known about. Landlord remains responsible for everything else in Section 12.`),o(`9. Move-in condition and possession`,`Within ${r(`checklist_days`)} days after move-in, Landlord and Tenant together complete and sign the Move-In/Move-Out Condition Checklist (Addendum 3), and each keeps a copy. It is used at move-out to decide deposit deductions.`,`If Landlord cannot deliver the Home on the start date, Tenant may cancel this lease in writing and get back all money paid, including any deposit, prepaid rent and application fee.`),o(`10. Pets and assistance animals`,i(`pets_allowed`)?`Pets allowed per the Pet & Assistance-Animal Addendum (Addendum 2).`:`No pets.`,`An assistance animal (a service animal or emotional-support animal needed because of a disability) is not a pet. Pet rules, pet fees and pet limits do not apply to it. See Addendum 2.`),o(`11. House rules`,`No smoking or vaping inside the Home${i(`no_smoking_property`)?` or anywhere on the property`:``}. No waterbeds. No swimming pools or trampolines. No dangerous amounts of gasoline, propane, kerosene, fireworks or similar (normal household and grill amounts are fine). No satellite dish mounted on the house (ground mount only). No stickers, nails or screws in walls without written OK${i(`picture_hooks_ok`)?` (small picture hooks are fine)`:``}. Do not flush wipes or pour grease down drains. No inoperable or unregistered vehicles or junk piles in the yard. Tenant follows noise and other local laws and creates no nuisance. Additional rules: ${r(`extra_rules`)}. New rules apply only if both parties sign them.`),o(`12. Repairs and upkeep`,`Landlord keeps the Home in a condition fit for living in and makes all repairs needed for that, except those Tenant causes. This includes the roof, structure, plumbing, electrical, heating, water heater, ${i(`ac_landlord`)?`air conditioning, `:``}and the appliances Landlord provides (subject to any initialed as-is list in Section 8).`,`Tenant:`,`(a) keeps the Home clean and sanitary;`,`(b) pays to repair damage caused by Tenant, occupants, guests or pets, beyond normal wear and tear;`,`(c) clears drain or toilet clogs Tenant causes;`,`(d) lawn: ${r(`lawn`)};`,`(e) replaces HVAC filters every ${r(`filter_days`)} days (Landlord supplies them: ${i(`filters_supplied`)?`yes`:`no`});`,`(f) replaces light bulbs;`,`(g) routine pest control is done by: ${r(`pest_control`)};`,`(h) takes trash out on collection days;`,`(i) keeps the Home reasonably ventilated, and in freezing weather drips faucets and covers outdoor spigots;`,`(j) reports in writing, without delay, any leak, water intrusion, mold, damage or needed repair, and is responsible for extra damage caused by not reporting.`,`How repairs happen: Tenant asks Landlord first (Section 21) and does not hire someone without asking, except in an emergency that threatens health, safety or serious property damage when Landlord cannot be reached. Landlord will repair within a reasonable time after Tenant's request. This lease does not take away any repair right Louisiana law gives Tenant if Landlord fails to repair within a reasonable time after demand.`,`Alterations: none without Landlord's written OK.`),o(`13. Smoke and carbon monoxide detectors`,`Before move-in, Landlord installs at least one working ten-year sealed lithium-battery smoke detector and at least one working sealed long-life-battery carbon monoxide detector (a combination unit is fine). Locations: ${r(`detector_locations`)}. Tenant tests them monthly, never removes or disables them, and reports any failure to Landlord in writing right away. Landlord replaces any unit that fails.`),o(`14. Landlord entry; locks`,`Landlord may enter with at least ${r(`entry_notice_hours`)} hours' notice, at reasonable times, to inspect, repair, or show the Home to buyers, lenders or new tenants. Landlord may enter without notice in an emergency. Tenant does not add or change locks without Landlord's written OK, and gives Landlord a key or code to any approved new lock. Landlord gives Tenant ${r(`key_count`)} keys, fobs or codes. Replacements cost ${r(`key_cost`)} each. All keys are returned at move-out, or the replacement cost is deducted.`),o(`15. Subletting and assignment`,`Tenant may not sublet, assign, or rent out any part of the Home (including short-term rentals) without Landlord's prior written consent. Consent once is not consent again.`),o(`16. Sale of the Home`,`If Landlord sells the Home, Landlord tells Tenant the new owner's or manager's contact information.`,i(`sale_ends_lease`)&&`The new owner may end this lease by written notice to Tenant at least ${r(`sale_notice_days`)} days in advance, and Tenant's deposit and any prepaid rent are then handled under Section 5.`),o(`17. Ending the lease early`,`Tenant's legal rights (always available, never with a fee):`,`- Military: an active or reserve servicemember (or their spouse) may end the lease under the federal Servicemembers Civil Relief Act (50 U.S.C. 3955) or La. R.S. 9:3261 (for example, change-of-station or deployment orders, discharge, or government quarters). They give written notice with a copy of the orders. No early termination charge applies.`,`- Sexual assault: a tenant who is a victim may end the lease under La. R.S. 9:3261.2 with the documentation that law requires.`,`- Domestic abuse: where La. R.S. 9:3261.1 applies (buildings of 6 or more units, with exceptions), a victim may end the lease under that law. This lease never limits or penalizes anyone for calling police or emergency help.`,i(`early_exit`)?`Optional paid early exit: Tenant may end a fixed-term lease early by giving at least ${r(`early_exit_days`)} days' written notice and paying an early-termination fee of ${r(`early_exit_fee`)}, plus rent through the move-out date. This option never applies to the legal rights listed above.`:`There is no paid early exit in this lease. The legal rights above always apply.`),o(`18. Storms, fire and other damage`,`If a fire, storm, hurricane, flood or other disaster not caused by Tenant:`,`(a) destroys the Home or makes it unlivable, the lease ends and rent stops as of that date;`,`(b) partly 